37749","name":"Extended synaptotagmin, C2B domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR037752","name":"Extended synaptotagmin, C-terminal C2 domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR037756","name":"Tricalbin, C2D domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR037761","name":"Tricalbin, C2A domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR037762","name":"Tricalbin, C2C domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR037765","name":"Tricalbin, C2B domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR037767","name":"Mug190-like, C2A domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR037768","name":"Copine, C2B domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR037772","name":"Freud, C2 domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR037775","name":"C2CD3, C2 domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR037778","name":"Protein kinase C-like, C2 domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR037784","name":"Serine/threonine-protein kinase N, C2 domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR037785","name":"C2CD5, C2 domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR037786","name":"Tandem C2 domains nuclear protein, C2A domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR037788","name":"Tandem C2 domains nuclear protein, C2B domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR037791","name":"Ingression protein 1, C2 domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR037795","name":"E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase HECW, C2 domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR041847","name":"Cytosolic phospholipase A2, C2 domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR043567","name":"Synaptotagmin-like 1-5, C2B domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR044750","name":"SRC2/BAP, C2 domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR047022","name":"Rabphilin/Doc2, first C2 domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR047255","name":"QUIRKY-like, fourth C2 domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR047257","name":"QUIRKY-like, second C2 domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR047258","name":"QUIRKY-like, third C2 domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR047897","name":"Synaptotagmins 15/17, C2A domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR057457","name":"CAPS, C2 domain","type":"Domain","children":[]},{"accession":"IPR057459","name":"SYDE1/2, C2 domain","type":"Domain","children":[]}]},"name":{"name":"C2 domain","short":"C2_dom"},"description":[{"text":"<p>The C2 domain is a Ca<sup>2+</sup>-dependent membrane-targeting module found in many cellular proteins involved in signal transduction or membrane trafficking. C2 domains are unique among membrane targeting domains in that they show wide range of lipid selectivity for the major components of cell membranes, including phosphatidylserine and phosphatidylcholine. This C2 domain is about 116 amino-acid residues and is located between the two copies of the C1 domain in Protein Kinase C and the protein kinase catalytic domain [[cite:PUB00081923]]. Regions with significant homology [[cite:PUB00002925]] to the C2-domain have been found in many proteins. The C2 domain is thought to be involved in calcium-dependent phospholipid binding [[cite:PUB00002815]] and in membrane targetting processes such as subcellular localisation.</p>\n\n<p>The 3D structure of the C2 domain of synaptotagmin has been reported [[cite:PUB00000918]], the domain forms an eight-stranded β-sandwich constructed around a conserved 4-stranded motif, designated a C2 key [[cite:PUB00000918]]. Calcium binds in a cup-shaped depression formed by the N- and C-terminal loops of the C2-key motif. Structural analyses of several C2 domains have shown them to consist of similar ternary structures in which three Ca<sup>2+</sup>-binding loops are located at the end of an 8 stranded antiparallel β-sandwich.</p>","llm":false,"checked":false,"updated":false}],"wikipedia":null,"literature":{"PUB00002925":{"PMID":7559667,"ISBN":null,"volume":"270","issue":"42","year":1995,"title":"Mammalian homologues of Caenorhabditis elegans unc-13 gene define novel family of C2-domain proteins.","URL":null,"raw_pages":"25273-80","medline_journal":"J Biol Chem","ISO_journal":"J. Biol. Chem.","authors":["Brose N","Hofmann K","Hata Y","Sudhof TC."],"DOI_URL":"http://dx.doi.org/10.1074/jbc.270.42.25273"},"PUB00002815":{"PMID":8253763,"ISBN":null,"volume":"268","issue":"35","year":1993,"title":"A single C2 domain from synaptotagmin I is sufficient for high affinity Ca2+/phospholipid binding.","URL":null,"raw_pages":"26386-90","medline_journal":"J Biol Chem","ISO_journal":"J. Biol. Chem.","authors":["Davletov BA","Sudhof TC."],"DOI_URL":"http://intl.jbc.org/cgi/content/abstract/268/35/26386"},"PUB00000918":{"PMID":7697723,"ISBN":null,"volume":"80","issue":"6","year":1995,"title":"Structure of the first C2 domain of synaptotagmin I: a novel Ca2+/phospholipid-binding fold.","URL":null,"raw_pages":"929-38","medline_journal":"Cell","ISO_journal":"Cell","authors":["Sutton RB","Davletov BA","Berghuis AM","Sudhof TC","Sprang SR."],"DOI_URL":"http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/0092-8674(95)90296-1"},"PUB00081923":{"PMID":22453964,"ISBN":null,"volume":"740","issue":null,"year":2012,"title":"The role of C2 domains in PKC signaling.","URL":null,"raw_pages":"663-83","medline_journal":"Adv Exp Med Biol","ISO_journal":"Adv. Exp. Med. Biol.","authors":["Farah CA","Sossin WS."],"DOI_URL":"http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/978-94-007-2888-2_29"}},"set_info":null,"overlaps_with":[{"accession":"IPR035892","name":"C2 domain superfamily","type":"homologous_superfamily"},{"accession":"IPR023315","name":"SynGAP C2 domain, N-terminal","type":"homologous_superfamily"}],"counters":{"subfamilies":0,"domain_architectures":5351,"interactions":31,"matches":495376,"pathways":809,"proteins":310184,"proteomes":3673,"sets":0,"structural_models":{"alphafold":213171},